# Model card: {{ project_name }}

What this model is, what it was trained on, and how well it did. Each
release publishes a copy of this page with the results filled in, beside
the model. Keep it true when you change the model or the data, the
metadata between the `---` lines at the top included: it is in the form
Hugging Face reads (license, library, tags).

## The model

- **What it does:** sorts an iris flower into one of three species from four
  measurements of its petals and sepals. Replace this line when you replace
  the model.
- **How it is made:** scikit-learn's logistic regression, trained by
  `python -m {{ package_name }} train` (`src/{{ package_name }}/train.py`).
- **How it is saved:** `model.skops`, in the skops format. Load it with
  `skops.io.load("model.skops")`, which refuses any type it was not told
  to trust. Never a pickle: loading one runs whatever code is inside it.
  Load it with the scikit-learn version the results name: another version
  may refuse the file or answer differently.
- **How to make it again:** the results name the commit, the seed and the
  SHA-256 of the training data (`data_sha256`, also in `metrics.json`).
  The same code, data and seed give the same model; a different data hash
  means the data was not the same.

## Intended use

- **What it is for:** learning how a model is trained, checked and
  released here, and a starting point to replace with your own. Say here
